  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">Against Marcion, written in its final form between 207 and 212, is Tertullian’s longest and most theologically ambitious work. Across five books he refutes the dualist theology of Marcion, who taught that the God of the Old Testament was an inferior creator-deity and that Christ came to reveal a previously unknown God of pure mercy. Tertullian defends the unity of the Creator and Redeemer, the goodness of creation, the authority of the Hebrew scriptures, and the integrity of the full biblical canon. It is his masterpiece.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
